	(text "Plugs into the 8-way socket on the back of the Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75 case.\nJ1 order matches the case label: 18 (SCL), 17 (SDA), 16, RX, TX, 3.3V, G, 5V. GPIO16, RX and TX are unused."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "00f15780-0a28-52e3-a2ea-b9cef3bedd4e")
	)
	(text "Harness faults (a wire at 14.4 V): R3/R5 limit clamp current to about 10 mA each into +3V3;\nD1/D2 hold the taps inside GND..VDD; D3 limits transients on the signal wire and does not conduct at 14.4 V.\nR1 then dissipates about 0.26 W, R3/R5 about 0.11 W each. The display board's load absorbs the rail current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 180.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "461190f1-0aa0-50c0-a62b-e1140fff03e6")
	)
	(text "5 V from a separate automotive 12 V -> 5 V converter enters on J2 pin 3; D4 stops USB-C power\nfeeding back into the converter when both are connected."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 167.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "89699f86-266e-58f6-80fd-a91571b32bb1")
	)
	(text "Ratiometric, differential measurement (hardware/WIRING.md):\nVp = AIN0 - AIN3 across R1 (Rp), Vs = AIN3 - AIN1 across the sender, Rs = Rp x Vs / Vp.\nLayout rules: R2 joins R1 pin 1 by its own trace (Kelvin), nothing in series between R1 and J2 pin 1,\nR3 and R5 tap the harness pins directly, R7 (break-detect bias) stays on the harness side of R5."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 167.64 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dab437bb-cf1a-54f6-b0fd-50665211c921")
	)
